course: dictionary
lesson: 12717
title: Dotted: many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one to use. Dotted is a good example. «The map had a dotted line from the castle to the lake.» Here dotted means marked with small dots, so the line is made of dots.
explain: «The meadow was dotted with yellow flowers.» Dotted with means having things spread here and there. The clue is the word flowers: they are scattered across the meadow, not lined up in a row. Ask yourself, what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: In music, dotted means something different. «The dotted note was held for a long time.» A dotted note lasts half as long again as the plain note. In a contract, «She signed on the dotted line» means she agreed to the paper and signed it.
fact: Dotted means marked with small dots, like «a dotted line».
fact: Dotted with means having small things spread here and there, like «a field dotted with sheep».
fact: In music, a dotted note lasts half as long again as the plain note.
fact: «Sign on the dotted line» means agree to and sign an official paper.
fact: The same word can have different meanings, so always check the words around it.
exercise: «Cut along the dotted line.» What does dotted line mean here? | A line painted in bright red | *A line made of small dots | A line that is very long | A wavy line drawn on the road
exercise: «The hillside was dotted with white sheep.» What does dotted with mean? | Painted with dots | *Spread here and there | Tied together with rope | Lined up in a row
exercise: Mia says, «He will sign on the dotted line tomorrow.» What does this mean? | *Agree to and sign an official paper | Draw dots on a page | Practise a song for a concert | Fall asleep on a line
test: «The dotted note lasts longer than a plain note.» In music, dotted means: | A note that is sung twice | A note with no sound at all | *A note that lasts half as long again | A note played very quietly
test: «The garden was dotted around with red and blue pots.» Dotted around means: | Painted all one colour | Tied to a fence | *Spread here and there | Hidden under the grass
exam: «The teacher drew the box with dotted lines for the hidden edges.» What do the dotted lines show? | *Edges you cannot see from this side | The box is wet | Where the box should be cut in half | Where the box is painted
